            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The remaining length is 95% of the original after the first machining, then 99.5% of that length after the second.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $x$ m be the original length. After the first machining, the length is $\\frac{19x}{20}$ m. After the second machining, $\\frac{199}{200}$ of that length remains.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{199}{200}\\times\\frac{19x}{20}&=3\\\\\\frac{3781x}{4000}&=3\\\\3781x&=12000\\\\x&=\\frac{12000}{3781}=3\\frac{657}{3781}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe first machining removes\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{100}\\times\\frac{12000}{3781}&=\\frac{600}{3781}\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe length after the first machining is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{19}{20}\\times\\frac{12000}{3781}&=\\frac{600}{199}\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe second machining removes\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{0.5}{100}\\times\\frac{600}{199}&=\\frac{3}{199}\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus the machining lengths are $\\frac{600}{3781}$ m and $\\frac{3}{199}$ m, respectively, and the original length is $3\\frac{657}{3781}$ m.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
